From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rahul Pon <theflyingrahul@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 22:04:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2711/2713] arm64: dts: qcom: Add the HP OmniBook 5 16-bf1xxx

Add a device tree for the HP OmniBook 5 16-bf1xxx (2026), with the
Snapdragon X2 Plus X2P-64-100 on the Mahua SoC. It describes the
keyboard, touchpad and touchscreen, the eDP OLED panel, the GPU, the
audio and compute DSPs, PMIC GLink for the battery and both USB-C
ports, the USB-A port, the camera's USB controller, the NVMe drive and
the Wi-Fi card, the QCC2072 Bluetooth and the embedded controller.

This is Rahul Pon's daily device tree as his linux-hp-omnibook-5-glymur
repository has it, which has no sign-off. It is written against
Qualcomm's qcom-next tree.

Link: https://github.com/theflyingrahul/linux-hp-omnibook-5-glymur/tree/ca32454d2ae69f52542670430d4726ed0de6bac6/dts/qcom
Signed-off-by: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
---
 .../dts/qcom/mahua-hp-omnibook-5-bf1xxx.dts   | 386 +++++++++++++++
 .../dts/qcom/mahua-hp-omnibook-5-bf1xxx.dtsi  | 453 ++++++++++++++++++
